Fixtures for the coaching-input contract crate (R2 Task 2, ADR-R2-2). Both files come from the
M3 worktree (branch m3, packages/ai), our own code, at commit
4ff8220aed41afb2dd23e04314511f6ebcb1f8e7 ("Merge M3 A3 (reference): reference tokens, leak
detector, evidence index"). Exported on 2026-11-21.

ts-schema.json
  z.toJSONSchema(CoachingInput, { target: "draft-2020-12", unrepresentable: "any" }) of
  packages/ai/src/input/schema.ts, with zod 4.6 (lockfile), Node v22.23.5, pnpm 12.21.0.
  sha256 361ee9f944b38a16f30989133afc83b223063a4268957588bdd82aa654ebfef8
  The zod refinements (superRefine, refine: FEN validity, side to move, unit ranges, low <= high,
  posterior inside the interval, events <= opportunities, unique ranks, each area once, onset
  order, analysed <= imported, windowStart <= windowEnd) are not exported; CoachingInput::validate
  covers them.

  The workspace has no tsx, and installing Linux node_modules into the m3 checkout would replace
  its host node_modules. So the sources were copied inside the container (read-only mount) and
  the export ran with Node's type stripping. With the m3 checkout at that commit:

    # export-schema.mts
    import { z } from "zod";
    import { CoachingInput } from "./src/input/schema.ts";
    console.log(JSON.stringify(
      z.toJSONSchema(CoachingInput, { target: "draft-2020-12", unrepresentable: "any" }),
      null, 2));

    # run.sh
    set -e
    mkdir /w
    cd /src && tar --exclude=node_modules --exclude=.git -cf - . | tar -xf - -C /w
    cd /w && corepack enable && pnpm install --frozen-lockfile >&2
    cp /scripts/export-schema.mts /w/packages/ai/ && cd /w/packages/ai
    node --experimental-strip-types export-schema.mts

    docker run --rm -v <m3 checkout>:/src:ro -v <dir with the two scripts>:/scripts:ro \
      node:22-slim sh /scripts/run.sh > backend/fixtures/coaching-input/ts-schema.json

  Refresh: rerun the command against the new m3 commit, update the commit, date and sha256
  above, then run the coaching-input tests (parity.rs). A shape change in the TS contract fails
  schemars_schema_matches_ts_schema_shape until the Rust types follow.

